---
source: crates/fosscut-mcp/tests/server.rs
expression: listing
---
[
  {
    "description": "Level the loudness of clips with sound: each clip is measured as it plays (its speed and sound effects applied) with the ITU-R BS.1770 meter on this machine, and its volume is set so it reaches target_lufs (default -14, the short-form platform level) with peaks under ceiling_dbfs (default -1). Where a clip's peaks leave too little room, or it needs more than the volume's +20 dB, an audio.limiter (gain and ceiling) makes up the rest unless limit is false. Silent clips keep their volume; clips with volume keyframes are refused. One undoable step with expected_revision, dry_run and request_id; returns each clip's measured loudness, peak, gain, new volume, limiter and the loudness it reaches.",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "ceiling_dbfs": {
          "description": "Highest sample peak in dBFS, from -12 to 0; -1 when omitted.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "clips": {
          "description": "The clips with sound to level (audio, video or compound clips).",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "dry_run": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Report what would change without committing it.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "expected_revision": {
          "description": "Fail with `fosscut.revision.conflict` unless the project is at this revision.",
          "format": "uint64",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Add or adjust an `audio.limiter` where the peaks leave too little room for the\nvolume alone (the default); false only changes volumes.",
          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "project": {
          "description": "Path of a `.fosscut` bundle; the open project when omitted.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "reason": {
          "description": "Why, recorded in the project's history.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "request_id": {
          "description": "Retry key.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "target_lufs": {
          "description": "Target loudness in LUFS; -14 (short-form platforms) when omitted; podcasts use -16.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "clips"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "audio_normalize",
    "read_only": false
  },
  {
    "description": "Edits measured from media on this machine, applied as one undoable step with expected_revision, dry_run and request_id. action split_scenes splits clip at its shot cuts (measured once and cached), so each shot is a clip of its own. action stabilize measures how the camera moved in clip and keys its transform.position, rotation and scale to cancel the shake (strength 0 to 1, default 0.5; up to 3 for a locked-off look), with one zoom up to 1.5 that hides the moving edges; it replaces those keyframes. action track follows region of clip (centre and size as fractions of the picture as it shows at at, found with frame_grab) from at to the clip's end, keying either mask (a mask of the clip: its centre follows) or follow (another clip such as a title or sticker: it moves as the region does from where it is); where the region is lost its last position holds and lost lists the ranges. action multicam makes a multicam clip of angles (video assets recorded at the same time, at least two): a compound timeline with each angle on its own track, lined up by offsets measured from their sound (unless offsets are given or sync is false; max_offset_seconds limits the search), one angle's sound (sound, from 1), placed at start; cut between angles afterwards with edit and the command multicam.switch. action multicam_sync only measures the offsets and their confidence (below 0.3 is doubtful). Framing follows a subject from cached analyses (run media_analyze first: [\"pose\"] for subject person, the default, or [\"matte\"] for any; [\"scenes\"] to frame shot by shot, unless shots is false): action reframe moves a crop of its timeline's shape over clip, so footage of another aspect follows its subject, or follows region from at; action camera_track zooms clip by zoom (1 to 4, default 1.5) on its own canvas and keeps the camera on the subject; action vertical copies timeline (the primary one by default) onto a width by height canvas (1080 by 1920) as a new timeline named name, every video clip following its subject and any without one left centred and listed. action beat_markers measures the beats of the music clip (once, cached; bpm when the tempo is known) and adds a marker on every every-th beat, counted from the first downbeat (4 marks bars); action beat_cuts moves each cut between the clips of track onto the nearest counted beat within tolerance, as roll edits, and lists the cuts it left with why. action short_candidates scores stretches of whole sentences of clip's cached transcript (min_seconds to max_seconds, default 15 to 60; count, default 10) by speech density, pauses, loudness, shot cuts and whether they stand alone, with the reasons and their media and timeline spans; action make_short builds a new vertical timeline of from to to of clip's media (a candidate's start and end), following its subject shot by shot, captioned from the transcript (captions, caption_preset) with an optional title. Returns the measurement and the response; check with frame_grab or contact_sheet.",
    "input": {
      "$defs": {
        "AutoEditAction": {
          "description": "What the `auto_edit` tool does.",
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "const": "split_scenes",
              "description": "Split a video clip at its scene changes.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "stabilize",
              "description": "Steady a shaky video clip.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "track",
              "description": "Make a mask or another clip follow a region of a video clip's picture.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "multicam",
              "description": "Make a multicam clip from angles recorded at the same time, lined up by their sound.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "multicam_sync",
              "description": "Only measure how far apart angles recorded at the same time started.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "reframe",
              "description": "Make a clip follow its subject on its timeline's canvas (another aspect).",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "camera_track",
              "description": "Keep the camera on a moving subject, zoomed in on the clip's own canvas.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "vertical",
              "description": "Copy a timeline onto a vertical canvas with every video clip following its subject.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "beat_markers",
              "description": "Put markers on the beats of a music clip.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "beat_cuts",
              "description": "Move the cuts between a track's clips onto the beats of a music clip.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "short_candidates",
              "description": "Score segments of a long clip that could stand alone as shorts.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "make_short",
              "description": "Build a vertical short from a range of a clip's media.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "FramingOptions": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Options of a framing.",
          "properties": {
            "dead_zone": {
              "default": 0.1,
              "description": "How far the subject may move from the crop's centre before the camera follows, as a\nfraction of the crop's width (or height, vertically), 0 to 0.4 (default 0.1).",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "ease_seconds": {
              "default": 0.5,
              "description": "How long a pan takes to start and to stop, in seconds, 0 to 3 (default 0.5).",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "headroom": {
              "default": 0.08,
              "description": "Room above the subject, as a fraction of the crop's height, 0 to 0.4 (default 0.08).",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "max_speed": {
              "default": 1.0,
              "description": "The fastest pan, in crop widths (or heights) per second, 0.05 to 10 (default 1).",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "max_zoom": {
              "default": 1.0,
              "description": "The most zoom chosen automatically, from `min_zoom` to 4 (default 1, so the crop\nonly pans).",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "min_zoom": {
              "default": 1.0,
              "description": "The least zoom, 1 or more (default 1: the largest crop of the target aspect).",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "padding": {
              "default": 0.15,
              "description": "Room around the subject when choosing the zoom, as a fraction of its size, 0 to 1\n(default 0.15).",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "zoom": {
              "description": "A fixed zoom from 1 to 4, instead of choosing one per shot.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": [
                "number",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "type": "object"
        },
        "RegionArg": {
          "description": "A region of a picture: its centre and size as fractions of the picture.",
          "properties": {
            "height": {
              "description": "The height, 0 to 1.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "width": {
              "description": "The width, 0 to 1.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "x": {
              "description": "The centre's distance from the left edge, 0 to 1.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "y": {
              "description": "The centre's distance from the top edge, 0 to 1.",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "x",
            "y",
            "width",
            "height"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "TimeInput": {
          "description": "A time with an explicit unit. Frame and timecode values use the timeline frame rate. Bare numbers are rejected.",
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "frames": {
                  "type": "integer"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "frames"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "seconds": {
                  "description": "Decimal seconds, for example \"3.9333\"",
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "number"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "seconds"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "timecode": {
                  "description": "HH:MM:SS:FF, or HH:MM:SS;FF for drop-frame",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "timecode"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "flicks": {
                  "type": "integer"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "flicks"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "description": "Shorthand: 118f, 3.9333s, 00:00:03:28 or 2775360000fl",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "action": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/AutoEditAction",
          "description": "`split_scenes`, `stabilize`, `track`, `multicam`, `multicam_sync`, `reframe`,\n`camera_track`, `vertical`, `beat_markers`, `beat_cuts`, `short_candidates` or\n`make_short`."
        },
        "angles": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "multicam, multicam_sync: the angles' video asset ids, at least two, in order; the\nfirst shows at the start.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "at": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/TimeInput"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "track: the timeline time where `region` is given; the clip's start when omitted."
        },
        "bpm": {
          "description": "beat_markers, beat_cuts: the music's tempo when known, in beats per minute, instead of\nestimating it.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "caption_preset": {
          "description": "make_short: the caption preset, such as `bold-pop`.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "captions": {
          "description": "make_short: caption the spoken words (default true).",
          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "clip": {
          "description": "split_scenes, stabilize, track, reframe, camera_track, short_candidates, make_short:\nthe video clip to measure.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "count": {
          "description": "short_candidates: see min_seconds.",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "dry_run": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Report what would change without committing it.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "every": {
          "description": "beat_markers, beat_cuts: every how many beats (1 to 16; default 1).",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "expected_revision": {
          "description": "Fail with `fosscut.revision.conflict` unless the project is at this revision.",
          "format": "uint64",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "follow": {
          "description": "track: another clip, such as a title or sticker, that moves as the region does from\nwhere it is (motion tracking).",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "framing": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/FramingOptions"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "reframe, camera_track, vertical, make_short: how the crop follows (dead zone, speed,\nease, headroom, padding, zoom limits); the defaults pan smoothly at zoom 1."
        },
        "from": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/TimeInput"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "make_short: where the short starts and ends in the clip's media (a candidate's span)."
        },
        "height": {
          "description": "vertical, make_short: see width.",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "mask": {
          "description": "track: a mask of the clip whose centre follows the region (mask tracking).",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "max_offset_seconds": {
          "description": "multicam, multicam_sync: look at most this many seconds either way; any offset when\nomitted.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "max_seconds": {
          "description": "short_candidates: see min_seconds.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "min_seconds": {
          "description": "short_candidates: shortest and longest candidate, in seconds (15 and 60), and how\nmany to return (10).",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "music": {
          "description": "beat_markers, beat_cuts: the music clip.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "name": {
          "description": "multicam, vertical, make_short: the new timeline's name.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "offsets": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "multicam: each angle's start in the scene, in order; measured from their sound when\nomitted, unless sync is false.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/TimeInput"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "project": {
          "description": "Path of a `.fosscut` bundle; the open project when omitted.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "reason": {
          "description": "Why, recorded in the project's history.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "region": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/RegionArg"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "track: the region to follow at `at`, in the picture as it shows (find it with\nframe_grab)."
        },
        "request_id": {
          "description": "Retry key.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "shots": {
          "description": "reframe, vertical, make_short: frame each shot on its own at the cached scene cuts\n(default true; run media_analyze with analyzers [\"scenes\"] first), or false for one\nframing over the whole clip.",
          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "sound": {
          "description": "multicam: which angle's sound plays, by number from 1; the first when omitted.",
          "format": "uint",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "start": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/TimeInput"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "multicam: where the multicam clip starts; appended when omitted."
        },
        "strength": {
          "description": "stabilize: how much motion to remove, 0 (none) to 1 (very smooth), up to 3 for a\nlocked-off look; 0.5 when omitted.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "subject": {
          "description": "reframe, camera_track, vertical, make_short: what the picture follows: `person`\n(the cached pose analysis, the default) or `any` (whatever the cached matte keeps);\nmake_short also takes `centre` (no analysis needed). reframe and camera_track\nfollow `region` from `at` instead when it is given.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "sync": {
          "description": "multicam: false lines the angles up at their starts instead of measuring offsets.",
          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "timeline": {
          "description": "multicam: timeline for the multicam clip; vertical: the timeline to copy; the primary\ntimeline when omitted.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "title": {
          "description": "make_short: a title over the first seconds.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "to": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/TimeInput"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "make_short: see from."
        },
        "tolerance": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/TimeInput"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "beat_cuts: how far a cut may move; half the spacing of the beats that count when\nomitted."
        },
        "track": {
          "description": "multicam: track for the multicam clip; beat_cuts: the video track whose cuts move.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "width": {
          "description": "vertical, make_short: the canvas size in pixels; 1080 by 1920 when omitted.",
          "format": "uint32",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "zoom": {
          "description": "camera_track: how far to zoom in, 1 to 4 (default 1.5).",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "action"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "auto_edit",
    "read_only": false
  },
  {
    "description": "List what FossCut can do: every editing command and query with a summary, the engine operations, the analyzers, the models and whether each is installed, and the export presets this machine can encode. Before using a command the first time, call it with names (for example [\"clip.add\", \"text.add\"]) to get just those argument schemas; detail: full returns every schema and error code at once and is large.",
    "input": {
      "$defs": {
        "Detail": {
          "description": "How much `capabilities` and `timeline_read` include.",
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "const": "outline",
              "description": "Names and summaries only.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "normal",
              "description": "Everything except schemas.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "full",
              "description": "Everything, including JSON Schemas.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "detail": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Detail",
          "description": "`outline` (default) lists names and summaries; `full` adds every command's JSON\nSchema, the request and time schemas, and the error codes (large)."
        },
        "names": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "Only these commands and queries, each with its argument JSON Schema, for example\n`[\"clip.add\", \"text.add\"]`. Ask for the commands you are about to use.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "capabilities",
    "read_only": true
  },
  {
    "description": "Word-timed captions. action generate captions the clips of a track from their cached transcripts (run media_analyze with analyzers [\"transcript\"] first): words become pages of a few words on a caption track, styled by preset (bold-pop, highlight, karaoke or boxed) and style. action import adds pages from an SRT file, one per cue; action export writes a caption track to an SRT file. action translate translates a caption track into to (hu or en) with a local model (install opus-mt-en-hu or opus-mt-hu-en with models), as a second line under each page (mode bilingual) or in place of its words (mode replace); you may also translate pages yourself with edit and captions.edit. action dub speaks each page (or with translation its translation) with a local English voice (install kokoro-82m), one clip per page at its start on an audio track. generate, import, translate and dub are one undoable step with expected_revision, dry_run and request_id. Then change pages with edit (captions.edit) and the look with captions.style, and check frame_grab at a spoken word.",
    "input": {
      "$defs": {
        "CaptionsAction": {
          "description": "What the `captions` tool does.",
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "const": "generate",
              "description": "Caption the clips of a track from their cached transcripts.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "import",
              "description": "Add caption pages from an SRT file, one page per cue.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "export",
              "description": "Write a caption track to an SRT file.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "translate",
              "description": "Translate a caption track's pages with a local model (English and Hungarian).",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "dub",
              "description": "Speak each caption page with a local English voice on an audio track.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "TranscriptOptions": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Options of the `transcript` analyzer.",
          "properties": {
            "keep_fillers": {
              "default": true,
              "description": "Prompt the model to write fillers such as \"um\" instead of tidying them away\n(default true).",
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "language": {
              "description": "Spoken language as a two-letter code such as `en`; detected when omitted, and always\nEnglish with English-only (`.en`) models.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "min_pause_ms": {
              "default": 300,
              "description": "Gaps between words reported as pauses, in milliseconds (default 300).",
              "format": "uint32",
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "model": {
              "description": "Model name, for example `whisper-base.en`; the most capable installed speech model\nfor the language when omitted.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "action": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/CaptionsAction",
          "description": "`generate` (from transcripts), `import` (an SRT file), `export` (to an SRT file),\n`translate` or `dub`."
        },
        "allow_destructive": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Allow replacing captions or overwriting an existing file. Ask the user first.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "audio_track": {
          "description": "dub: the audio track for the speech; a new one when omitted.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "dry_run": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Report what would change without committing it (or, for export, without writing).",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "expected_revision": {
          "description": "Fail with `fosscut.revision.conflict` unless the project is at this revision.",
          "format": "uint64",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "file": {
          "description": "The SRT file to import or to write.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "lyrics": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "generate: caption a song's lyrics: the music track first, one sung line per page,\nthe karaoke look unless a preset is given.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "mode": {
          "description": "translate: `bilingual` (a second line under each page, the default) or `replace`\n(the page's words become the translation, spread over the page's time).",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "paging": {
          "description": "generate: paging limits, for example `{\"max_words\": 3, \"max_lines\": 1}`."
        },
        "preset": {
          "description": "A built-in look: `bold-pop`, `highlight`, `karaoke` or `boxed` (capabilities lists\nthem with descriptions).",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "project": {
          "description": "Path of a `.fosscut` bundle; the open project when omitted.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "reason": {
          "description": "Why, recorded in the project's history.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "replace": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Replace the caption track's existing captions; also needs allow_destructive.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "request_id": {
          "description": "Retry key for generate and import.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "skip_fillers": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "generate: leave out the words the transcript marks as fillers (\"um\", \"uh\").",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "source_track": {
          "description": "generate: the track whose clips are captioned; the first video or audio track with\nsound when omitted.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "speed": {
          "description": "dub: speaking speed from 0.5 to 2 (default 1).",
          "format": "float",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "style": {
          "description": "Changes to the caption track's look as a JSON merge patch, for example\n`{\"placement\": \"middle\", \"size\": 0.07}`."
        },
        "subtitles": {
          "description": "export: `original` (the default), `translation` (each page's translation line) or\n`both` (bilingual: the words, then the translation).",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "timeline": {
          "description": "Timeline; the primary timeline when omitted.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "to": {
          "description": "translate: the language to translate into, `hu` or `en`.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "track": {
          "description": "Caption track; the first caption track (created when adding) when omitted.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "transcript": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/TranscriptOptions",
          "default": {
            "keep_fillers": true,
            "min_pause_ms": 300
          },
          "description": "generate: the transcript options the media was analyzed with (`model`, `language`,\n`min_pause_ms`), if not the defaults."
        },
        "translation": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "dub: speak each page's translation instead of its words.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "voice": {
          "description": "dub: the voice, such as `af_heart`; see the record tool's action voices.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "action"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "captions",
    "read_only": false
  },
  {
    "description": "Automatic color for a video or image clip, measured from its frames on this machine. action auto adds a color.adjust effect (first in the clip's effects) that neutralizes the white balance, sets the brightness and stretches blacks and whites; action match adds one that brings the clip's balance, brightness, contrast and saturation close to the reference clip. One undoable step with expected_revision, dry_run and request_id; returns the measurements and the effect. Adjust the effect afterwards with edit (effect.set) and check frame_grab.",
    "input": {
      "$defs": {
        "ColorAction": {
          "description": "What the `color` tool does.",
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "const": "auto",
              "description": "Correct white balance, brightness and levels.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "const": "match",
              "description": "Bring the clip close to a reference clip.",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "action": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ColorAction",
          "description": "`auto` or `match`."
        },
        "clip": {
          "description": "The video or image clip to correct.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "dry_run": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Report what would change without committing it.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "expected_revision": {
          "description": "Fail with `fosscut.revision.conflict` unless the project is at this revision.",
          "format": "uint64",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "project": {
          "description": "Path of a `.fosscut` bundle; the open project when omitted.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "reason": {
          "description": "Why, recorded in the project's history.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "reference": {
          "description": "match: the clip whose look to match.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "request_id": {
          "description": "Retry key.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "action",
        "clip"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "color",
    "read_only": false
  },
  {
    "description": "Render frames spread evenly over the timeline into one PNG grid (default 12 frames, 240 pixels wide each), to check a whole edit at a glance. Returns the image and each tile's time and position.",
    "input": {
